# core §12.5.1 rule 6 — THE EXPONENT FORMS ARE REACHABLE.
#
# The value grammar is a plain decimal with no magnitude limit (§15.5), so
# a 22-digit coordinate is the double 1e21 and a seventh decimal place is
# 1e-7. ECMA-262 Number::toString writes both with an exponent, and the
# canonical model carries exactly that spelling: "x": 1e+21, "x": 1e-7.
# Until this release rule 6 called these forms unreachable.
figdown 0.5 block
node far "Far"
node near "Near"
pin far at=(1000000000000000000000,0)
pin near at=(0.0000001,20)
